# Pinned from the real red run of 2026-07-28. The second half of TASK-XPYRR's
# acceptance: a title edit must not be able to drop what else the heading line
# carries.
#
# The injection deletes the tag-preserving path in
# `OrgRewriter::edit_heading_line` — one line, `unwrap_or(current.tags)` becomes
# `unwrap_or_default()`. That is the whole defect. It is worth a separate proof
# from the missing-flag one because it fails in the opposite direction: the
# command SUCCEEDS. Exit 0, a tx recorded, a corrected title on the board, and
# four org tags gone. Nothing in the run says so.
#
# It also shows why the round-trip guard cannot be the detector here. The guard
# compares what was composed against what re-parses back, and under this
# injection both agree the heading has no tags — they were dropped before
# either was computed. Preservation is enforced by construction (the rewriter
# reads the tags off the pre-edit heading; the caller never gets to name them),
# so what proves it is a test that knew the tags beforehand.
exit: 101

# The heading line, both sides. The left is what the injection wrote; the right
# is what the fixture heading — shaped like TASK-0RCRY — is supposed to keep.
contains: heading must keep its level, TODO keyword, id token and tags
contains: :daemon:drivers:tmux:testing:

# The failure is the tag assertion, not an earlier one: `--title` still parses,
# still reaches the daemon, still rewrites the title. If a future edit breaks
# the flag itself the run falls earlier with a different message and this
# artifact has stopped reproducing what it claims.
contains: test result: FAILED. 0 passed; 1 failed
